    {
      "html": "<h1>Adaptive Systems Engineering (ASE-301)</h1><h2>Course Description</h2><p>Design of adaptive software and socio-technical systems that respond to changing environments, user behavior, and operational constraints.</p><h2>Learning Objectives</h2><ul style=\"list-style-type: none\"><li>• Model adaptive system behavior</li><li>• Analyze feedback loops and control strategies</li><li>• Design resilient architectures</li><li>• Evaluate system adaptation tradeoffs</li></ul><h2>Weekly Topics</h2><p>Week 1: Introduction to Adaptive Systems Week 2: Feedback Control Week 3: Runtime Monitoring<br/>Week 4: Self-Healing Architectures Week 5: Reinforcement Learning for Adaptation Week 6:<br/>Human-in-the-Loop Systems Week 7: Midterm Review Week 8: Distributed Adaptation Week 9:<br/>Fault Tolerance Week 10: Resource Optimization Week 11: Case Studies Week 12: Final Project<br/>Presentations</p><h2>Assessments</h2><p>Midterm Exam: 25% Lab Assignments: 25% Team Project: 35% Participation: 15%</p><h2>Prerequisites</h2><p>Software Engineering Fundamentals, Data Structures, Probability Basics</p>",
